[TITLE]
CON-11: storage unit SU1 (1000 ft2, 4 ft deep, no inflow, no outflow) holds
TSS = 100 mg/L and TP = 10 mg/L. TP has the concentration-type equation
C = 0.05*TSS; TSS has no equation. In a concentration-type equation TSS is
the node concentration before treatment (manual, section 5.4.2), so
TP = MIN(10, 0.05*100) = 5 mg/L for the whole run.

[OPTIONS]
FLOW_UNITS           CFS
FLOW_ROUTING         DYNWAVE
START_DATE           01/01/2020
START_TIME           00:00:00
REPORT_START_DATE    01/01/2020
REPORT_START_TIME    00:00:00
END_DATE             01/01/2020
END_TIME             01:00:00
DRY_STEP             00:05:00
WET_STEP             00:05:00
ROUTING_STEP         10
REPORT_STEP          00:15:00

[JUNCTIONS]
;;Name  Elev  MaxDepth  InitDepth  SurDepth  Aponded
J2      0     5         0          0         0

[OUTFALLS]
;;Name  Elev  Type
O1      0     FREE

[STORAGE]
;;Name  Elev  MaxDepth  InitDepth  Shape       Coeff  Expon  Const
SU1     0     10        4          FUNCTIONAL  0      0      1000

[CONDUITS]
;;Name  From  To  Length  Roughness  InOffset  OutOffset  InitFlow
C1      SU1   J2  400     0.013      11        0          0
C2      J2    O1  400     0.013      0         0          0

[XSECTIONS]
;;Link  Shape     Geom1  Geom2  Geom3  Geom4  Barrels
C1      CIRCULAR  1      0      0      0      1
C2      CIRCULAR  1      0      0      0      1

[POLLUTANTS]
;;Name  Units  Crain  Cgw  Crdii  Kdecay  SnowOnly  CoPollut  CoFrac  Cdwf  Cinit
TSS     MG/L   0      0    0      0       NO        *         0       0     100
TP      MG/L   0      0    0      0       NO        *         0       0     10

[TREATMENT]
;;Node  Pollutant  Function
SU1     TP         C = 0.05*TSS

[REPORT]
NODES ALL
LINKS ALL
